m/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T02:40:46-08:00","id":787243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=786966#post786966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good luck, one and all.<br /> <br /> God, it'd be so much fun to write for this.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then apply! Said it was an open call, so good luck!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T03:55:34-08:00","id":787260,"title":"","content":"I hope The Ascending Ones get fixed in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:00:59-08:00","id":787332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787243#post787243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then apply! Said it was an open call, so good luck!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I intend to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Raistlin: I'm not sure what you mean by fixed, but making the Ascending Ones awesome is one of the big things I want to work on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:14:46-08:00","id":787345,"title":"","content":"Curious minds inquring. I want to hear what you mean by the fixing Ascending Ones comment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787202#post787202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we also need to remember that Endowments and Tactics don't take the same space as Rotes and Arcana, the Code not being equivalent to Wisdom and that Risking Willpower is the only &quot;template ability&quot; Hunters get. I'm not saying that putting all the groups in the book would be easy (considering we also need a section about building your own monsters, because that is half of what Hunter is), but it may be done with a very clever design.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not sure why the force comparison to Mage, but I do want to comment about the building own monsters bit. The Chronicle of Darkness book already comes with a building own monster bit. So, there will probably be a reprint.<br /> <br /> I'm personally wondering, though, if we'll be getting Infernal rules along side the Slasher stuff, or if the Lucifuge will change around a bit. Actually, I'm kinda really excited about the Slasher stuff, and want to see what they do with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - I bet there will also be some working on the Code. If at least some suggestions. Integrity is really inappropriate for Hunters to use, IMHO. Integrity is a measurement for how well your santity can hold up against the terrors of the supernatural world, Call of Cthulhu style. Hunter's Code needs to be something that measures the difference between man and monster, and how far you've fallen from the former towards becoming one of the things you hunt. Honestly, I think we should have a complete swap out instead of maintaining Integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-16-2015, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:26:27-08:00","id":787350,"title":"","content":"I compared it to Mage because Hawthorn compared it to Mage. No need to get angry :P<br /> <br /> Also, I don't have CoD- I didn't thought it has anything interesting in it other than some summary of rule updates and such, so I didn't gave it any attention. Apparently, I was wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:31:10-08:00","id":787352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787243#post787243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then apply! Said it was an open call, so good luck!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think that Arcane meant that as he was going to get denied working on the project. Just that the Open Call is likely to be super, super competitive. I was planning on just trying to get Monica to let me write up Abu Dhabi and Dubai as settings, but now that all of the compacts and conspiracies could get included, I'm also gunning for writing the Ahl Al-Jabal. My girlfriend is Ismailii, so are tons of my friends, I have a degree in Islamic history, and lived in the Middle East for 3 years. I need to work on this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:31:48-08:00","id":787354,"title":"","content":"Not angry, just confused. But, yeah. I asked the same thing in a thread on the front page - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/784723-so-what-s-actually-in-the-chronicles-of-darkness\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...es-of-darkness</a><br /> <br /> In short, there's monster building section, there's new investigation (mental combat equivalent?), chases, and cracting rules, there's new merits, including new psychic stuff that's not in the rules update.<br /> <br /> Honestly, even the changes to the skills section, and the expanded and better defined social merits are something I'm going to invest in sometime after X-mas. Its a very sexy book from the sounds of it, even if its mortal only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:36:00-08:00","id":787358,"title":"","content":"Like, know that there's a lot of us who were already freelancers trying to wiggle our way into this book? And it sounds like Monica's keen to scoop up more new talent.<br /> <br /> That's exciting, but it also means trying to get on the job will be a clusterfuck. On top of that, freelancers who have done work before usually get in first, but I don't think that's happening this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:38:49-08:00","id":787359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787358#post787358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, know that there's a lot of us who were already freelancers trying to wiggle our way into this book? And it sounds like Monica's keen to scoop up more new talent.<br /> <br /> That's exciting, but it also means trying to get on the job will be a clusterfuck. On top of that, freelancers who have done work before usually get in first, but I don't think that's happening this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I love, because I'm not one of said freelancers, and I believe I have the chops to go toe to toe with them. But this is going to be INTENSE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:39:36-08:00","id":787362,"title":"","content":"Maybe, maybe not. I remember that the call for Hurt Locker focused on new talent over someone not approved before. This could be similar to get as many people with their foot in the door as possible, and as many fresh ideas as possible. We don't want the CoD to be an incestious group think. Variety, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T07:55:23-08:00","id":787373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787362#post787362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, maybe not. I remember that the call for Hurt Locker focused on new talent over someone not approved before. This could be similar to get as many people with their foot in the door as possible, and as many fresh ideas as possible. We don't want the CoD to be an incestious group think. Variety, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the way you think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T09:11:41-08:00","id":787419,"title":"","content":"Like I said, exciting, and I think I'm among the new enough crowd to have that going for me. But still, busy busy times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T11:56:05-08:00","id":787536,"title":"","content":"I was on the fence before, but with this announcement I have carved out an app for Hunter 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:12:53-08:00","id":788379,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping that the authors' reading lists include <b>World of Darkness: Dogs of War</b> (for its section on coping with PTSD) and <b>World of Darkness: Asylum</b> (for its section on therapy): assuming that <b>Hunter</b> keeps Integrity as its \u201cTheme Trait\u201d, which I think is a safe assumption, guidelines for protecting against Integrity loss and for restoring lost Integrity are likely to be <i>very</i> important, more so than in 1e (where you didn't risk degeneration merely by encountering horrific things). Granted, the aforementioned books were written with a Morality trait in mind; but the advice they give strikes me as <i>at least</i> as appropriate for Integrity as it was for Morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T16:34:40-08:00","id":788396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=788379#post788379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping that the authors' reading lists include <b>World of Darkness: Dogs of War</b> (for its section on coping with PTSD) and <b>World of Darkness: Asylum</b> (for its section on therapy): assuming that <b>Hunter</b> keeps Integrity as its \u201cTheme Trait\u201d, which I think is a safe assumption, guidelines for protecting against Integrity loss and for restoring lost Integrity are likely to be <i>very</i> important, more so than in 1e (where you didn't risk degeneration merely by encountering horrific things). Granted, the aforementioned books were written with a Morality trait in mind; but the advice they give strikes me as <i>at least</i> as appropriate for Integrity as it was for Morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see some serious cribbing from Touchstones, or the Bonds system in the mew Delta Green. You might be a Hunter, but you're also a real person ostensibly doing this to keep the people you care about safe. Are you going to tell your wife that you hunt vampires, or are you going to leave her wondering why you don't come home some nights? What do your coworkers think when you have to take time off because of the bullet wound you can't explain?<br /> <br /> Turn the grit up to eleven, but retain the fundamentally human factor of things. Hammer home that you can either have a functional life or the Vigil, but not both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T22:00:44-08:00","id":789111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787352#post787352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't think that Arcane meant that as he was going to get denied working on the project. Just that the Open Call is likely to be super, super competitive. I was planning on just trying to get Monica to let me write up Abu Dhabi and Dubai as settings, but now that all of the compacts and conspiracies could get included, I'm also gunning for writing the Ahl Al-Jabal. My girlfriend is Ismailii, so are tons of my friends, I have a degree in Islamic history, and lived in the Middle East for 3 years. I need to work on this!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be very excited to see this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=788396#post788396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd like to see some serious cribbing from Touchstones, or the Bonds system in the mew Delta Green. You might be a Hunter, but you're also a real person ostensibly doing this to keep the people you care about safe. Are you going to tell your wife that you hunt vampires, or are you going to leave her wondering why you don't come home some nights? What do your coworkers think when you have to take time off because of the bullet wound you can't explain?<br /> <br /> Turn the grit up to eleven, but retain the fundamentally human factor of things. Hammer home that you can either have a functional life or the Vigil, but not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think Vigil is actually a really good place to put emphasis on additional Anchors besides Virtue &amp; Vice for mortal characters. Perhaps the updated version of the Code might interact with them, and help mark Hunters as being distinct from mortals? I think Bonds in the new Delta Green do great in specifically modeling this relationship, and given the direction that the games have taken in design, I think it'd make great sense to do so for Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:23:29-08:00","id":790335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=787179#post787179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whoa...thats a lot of content. Is Hunter going to outstrip Mage for page count?<br /> <br /> Anyway, rage against the dying of the light and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mage 2e is slightly shorter than Promethean 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T10:41:43-08:00","id":790345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=790335#post790335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mage 2e is slightly shorter than Promethean 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diggity dang, certainly did not expect that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T02:59:20-08:00","id":790775,"title":"","content":"I would want to hear form you about elephant in the room with now Chronicles of Darkness coming out...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyrdhamster's question</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">With now publishing of Chronicle of Darkness corebook, with it\u2019s rules on Professional Training and monster creation ( as Horrors with Dread Powers ) what Hunter 2ED can offer in comparison to plain CoD for the Tier 1 hunters?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Because now difference between Tier 1 hunters and mortals investigators ( from CoD ) is just semantics. ALL the rules needed from Hunter 1ED are in CoD corebook\u2026</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Monica answered me with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monica's answer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In addition to Tactics and a few other tweaks, there are substantive setting differences. The Chronicles of Darkness rulebook features The God Machine Chronicle. While the rules are a fantastic foundation for Hunter, the big setting differences are the fact that your average rank-and-file hunting monsters doesn\u2019t necessarily mean that player-character is a hunter. Hunters already know that there are monsters lurking in the darkness, and they each uphold the Vigil in their own unique way. Hunter 2E will also feature the Slasher Chronicle, and that will shape tiered play. Right now, I\u2019m going to propose some changes to Tier Two and Tier Three styles of play, but I will also be taking a look at enhancing Tier One as well. That\u2019s a ways off, however, because the setting is more substantive for compacts and conspiracies, and I\u2019d like to address some possibilities before nailing down an approach.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I do not think it's enough alternative, taking even in account Code as Integrity analog, Tactics or Slashers. It still all rattles in mine head &quot;it's just mortals, not hunters&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:19:06-08:00","id":790908,"title":"","content":"This is just the way I run things, but in my games, all Hunters have some supernatural talent or another. They may have a Minor Template, or a supernatural merit, the Forbidden Lore from Mirrors, an Endowment, it doesn't matter. What matters is that this differentiates proper Hunters from mortals who go delving into the supernatural for fun and profit. That's just how I run things. Hunters may still qualify as mortals, but they're metaphysically different, and the universe can tell (for example, if a ward allows you to select a type of creature to keep at bay, &quot;Hunters&quot; and &quot;mortals&quot; will be two different types of creatures, even though Hunters are also technically mortals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T03:21:38-08:00","id":792687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=790775#post790775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would want to hear form you about elephant in the room with now Chronicles of Darkness coming out...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Monica answered me with this:<br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> I do not think it's enough alternative, taking even in account Code as Integrity analog, Tactics or Slashers. It still all rattles in mine head &quot;it's just mortals, not hunters&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>But Hunters <i>are</i> just mortals. They may dedicate themselves to hunting monsters, but unless they actually possess some supernatural trait of their own they are <i>just</i> normal humans. The only thing they really have to set them apart is proper training, information, equipment, and dedication to this particular cause. That's it. That's all a Hunter really is, and imo there really <i>shouldn't</i> be much that inherently sets them apart from normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T21:08:03-08:00","id":793931,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with there being <i>optional</i> rules (designed primarily with Tier 2+ in mind) that can make hunters more template-like if the Storyteller is more interested in portraying hunters as something special (e.g., the Heroic Mortal \u201ctemplate\u201d from <b>Strange Dead Love</b>; the \u201cExtraordinary Mortals\u201d Skill Tricks from <b>Mirrors</b>; the \u201cextra uses for Willpower\u201d, also from <b>Mirrors</b>; and <i>maybe</i> even Conviction from the same source); but such things should be left <i>strictly</i> In the realm of optional rules. The <i>only</i> mechanical benefit that hunters should have that mortals lack is Practical Experience; and even <i>its</i> benefits should be tailored according to the style of game the Storyteller is after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T21:31:42-08:00","id":793941,"title":"","content":"We can also... you know... wait to see what the Open Dev process ends up with since Monica has said she's going to look at all Tiers to see about there being a bit more of a line between playing mortals with CofD and playing Tier 1 and Tier 2 HtV<br /> <br /> I personally think it's worth exploring. While I agree that Tier 1 and Tier 2 shouldn't move beyond mortals, I think some additional default mechanical weight (so far we have extra WP options, and PXP to get Tactics) to being a hunter wouldn't be a bad thing. Tier 2 is actually where I find HtV the weakest until Compacts and Conspiracies (and then it's &quot;optional&quot; and therefore harder to sell).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=792687#post792687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing they really have to set them apart is proper training, information, equipment, and dedication to this particular cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, this. Right now, this basically doesn't have a strong representation in the base-line game. Hunters have access to slightly better training (PXP for Tactics), and the additional WP options are sort of dedication to the cause, but unless you're in Tier 3 play, this isn't well represented; esp. at start vs. as progress.<br /> <br /> I also think the 2e mechanics have a lot to offer in this regard. All hunters, like werewolves, could have access to some sort of Hunt Conditions with Tier scaled benefits as something that just sprung to my mind. Call it &quot;Keeping the Vigil,&quot; and have a few options for different types of Hunts. It never has to be supernatural, but there's a lot of things that could be done with it to make hunters feel a bit more capable without ditching the themes of Tier 1-2 play, and still apply to Tier 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T22:08:57-08:00","id":793955,"title":"","content":"The play distinction has always been sharp in my mind. Mortals <i>live</i> with the darkness, Hunters <i>do something about it or with it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T23:11:10-08:00","id":793978,"title":"","content":"While that functions as a thematic difference, I don't think it holds true &quot;in the wild&quot; of play. Players want to play characters that do something, not characters that live with something.<br /> <br /> If I'm running a haunt house sort of story, how to I actualize the difference between &quot;living with the ghosts,&quot; vs. &quot;doing something about the ghosts,&quot; for mortals vs. Tier 1 hunters, while account for the fact that my players are going to want their characters to do something about the haunting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T23:21:44-08:00","id":793987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=793955#post793955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The play distinction has always been sharp in my mind. Mortals <i>live</i> with the darkness, Hunters <i>do something about it or with it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters as mortal investigators in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> are also <i>doing something about</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />They investigate and solve cases, sometimes kills Horror or banish ghost or spirit. ( It's all in the rules and encouraged by the corebook )<br /> <br /> <i>How </i>it is different from Tier 1 <b>Hunter</b>? I even rephrase a question - <i>How </i>it is different from<b> Supernatural</b> Monster of the Week episode? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mine own answer could be this - <b>Hunters have Code</b>. Their Integrity do not slide like crazy in confrontation with Unknown, but they also<i> risking becoming Slashers</i> ( by evolution of Code ). This could really different Tier 1 play from mortal investigators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-28-2015, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T04:39:12-08:00","id":794093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=793987#post793987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>How </i>it is different from Tier 1 <b>Hunter</b>? I even rephrase a question - <i>How </i>it is different from<b> Supernatural</b> Monster of the Week episode? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mortals do their thing, and when it stops bothering them, go back to their normal lives. A hunter doesn't, as the vigil encompasses the rest of their life. Plus there's the issue of direction. Mortals generally only investigate things that affect them directly, while hunters, when not being affected personally, seek out issues to investigate.<br /> <br /> That said, all hunters don't 'hunt.' Many of the compacts are more about gathering information or dealing with other issues instead of going out and attacking the supernatural. Perhaps some of these groups should be altered in second edition so as to either become more clearly hunters or more clearly not, especially since there's more mechanical support for things like mystery cults and not everything has to be a compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T08:53:20-08:00","id":794206,"title":"","content":"My take on it is that a mortal who faces the supernatural gets a choice (sometimes consciously, sometimes subconsciously): If you choose to accept the supernatural, you become a Hunter. If you choose to reject it, you remain a mortal.<br /> <br /> It's not about what you do (both hunter and mortal may take out that Slasher or resolve the haunting in the house), but about why you do it. The mortal deals with it so that he can go back to his normal life, where he'll try the hardest to forget it (and most of the time, he will, since the CofD cast a veil of haziness over this sort of thing). The hunter deals with it and then keeps hunting the supernatural down, because she has to do something about it. She can't go back to her life now that she's seen the truth of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:25:49-08:00","id":794258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794093#post794093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mortals do their thing, and when it stops bothering them, go back to their normal lives. A hunter doesn't, as the vigil encompasses the rest of their life. Plus there's the issue of direction. Mortals generally only investigate things that affect them directly, while hunters, when not being affected personally, seek out issues to investigate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:47:00-08:00","id":794295,"title":"","content":"But from the gameplay experience mortal investigators and Tier 1 hunters play the same - they have &quot;case&quot;, they study monster, the solve it. Their motivation <i>does not</i> change <u>the story</u>, none the bit.<br /> <br /> P.S. I agree totally with <b>Heavy Arms</b> post below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-28-2015, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:57:43-08:00","id":794304,"title":"","content":"I feel that's a fairly weak response; mostly because it really doesn't seem to mesh with trying to run a long term mortals focused game. It's basically saying that all long term mortal games will turn into Tier 1 hunters, because after the nth time they've dealt with something supernatural and decided to stop being 100% reactive about the existence of more supernaturals out there, they're hunters. If you want to keep to a mortals game thematically... you have to make all the PCs stupid so they'll never start taking proactive steps to protect their normal life from the supernatural stuff they've encountered; lest they become a Tier 1 hunter for it.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons I thought of something like having something similar to the Sacred Hunt Conditions from Forsaken to give to hunters. Rather than some arbitrary line of reactive vs.proactive approach to the existence of the supernatural, hunters take dealing with the supernatural an extra step that's represented in how those Conditions are generated, and what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:19:04-08:00","id":794318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794295#post794295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But from the gameplay experience mortal investigators and Tier 1 hunters play the same - they have &quot;case&quot;, they study monster, the solve it. Their motivation <i>does not</i> change <u>the story</u>, none the bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually does I think. Usually standard mortals games require a degree of lead-in. You need to set up a story as to where you are and why you've gotten involved. Hunter allows you to skip to the investigation. Why are you hunting something? You're a hunter. Easy.<br /> <br /> I personally don't really care for the thematic differences between mortals and Hunters. They tend to fall over extremely quickly and I don't find them all that interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:50:04-08:00","id":794338,"title":"","content":"Mortals are victims of the darkness. Hunters seek it out.<br /> <br /> That's the core thematic difference between the two; in a world where horrible things lurk in the shadows and the average person is mostly concerned with keeping their head down, Hunters are the crazy few who actively search for the horrors at the heart of the setting. Mortals stumble across terrible things, or try to escape the, so that they can resume their normal lives; Hunters want to fight back, to reveal the truth, to protect others instead of saving their own skin. The Vigil destroys your body and mind, shatters and illusion of a mundane existence you might've once had... but it's an ibsession that keeps draeing you back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:52:51-08:00","id":794339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794295#post794295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But from the gameplay experience mortal investigators and Tier 1 hunters play the same - they have &quot;case&quot;, they study monster, the solve it. Their motivation <i>does not</i> change <u>the story</u>, none the bit.<br /> <br /> P.S. I agree totally with <b>Heavy Arms</b> post below.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because there isn't really much of a difference between a Tier 1 Hunter and your normal everyday person. The only thing separating them is their skill set. A Hunter should tend to have skills and merits to help them Hunt monsters whereas Average Joe Normalguy has a skill set appropriate to whatever his chosen profession is. Sometimes there's a bit of overlap, maybe Joe Normalguy hunts (lower case animal hunter) as a hobby, so he might be a pretty good shot and be skilled at tracking and sneaking up on his prey. That would transfer over nicely if he ever became a capital H Hunter. <br /> <br /> So again, at least as far as Tier 1 is concerned, the only thing that really separates the two comes down to build, motivation, and their reaction to situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T12:56:20-08:00","id":794341,"title":"","content":"And risking Willpower, and the chance to develop The Code...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T13:07:52-08:00","id":794345,"title":"","content":"There's also the setting element. Hunter pretty clearly gives the impression that there's something approaching a Hunter subculture which isn't really present for mortals. You may be a Tier 1 Hunter, but you can fairly reasonably come in contact with members of Tier 2 groups and even Tier 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T13:08:34-08:00","id":794347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794304#post794304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that's a fairly weak response; mostly because it really doesn't seem to mesh with trying to run a long term mortals focused game. It's basically saying that all long term mortal games will turn into Tier 1 hunters, because after the nth time they've dealt with something supernatural and decided to stop being 100% reactive about the existence of more supernaturals out there, they're hunters. If you want to keep to a mortals game thematically... you have to make all the PCs stupid so they'll never start taking proactive steps to protect their normal life from the supernatural stuff they've encountered; lest they become a Tier 1 hunter for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the movie Poltergeist, they realize something supernatural is happening in their home, things escalate, and in the end, they move and get rid of their tv, potentially living the rest of their lives, except for arguably some sequels, without involving the supernatural except perhaps tangentially. Fox Mulder, on the other hand, had an experience when he was a child and spent the rest of his life aggressively seeking the cause and other parallel issues.<br /> <br /> Hunters actively seek out the supernatural and put an end to its interference in things. Mortals try to live mortal lives, hunters don't. You can play long-term mortal games all you want, but if your characters are supernatural investigators, you would be better served by playing Hunter, that's what the game is for and there's more support for them within the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794341#post794341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And risking Willpower, and the chance to develop The Code...</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the detachment of Integrity to Morality it doesn't seem like the Code would really matter, unless it becomes its own Morality system, which the rest of the Chronicles of Darkness seem to shrug off. Integrity has some vestiges that could conceivably be tied to Morality, 'What's the worst thing you could imagine doing?' but they are really not about how bad a thing is as much as the shock of breaking your personal beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-28-2015, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T13:20:48-08:00","id":794354,"title":"","content":"One thing that the upcoming edition of Delta Green stresses is the toll that hunting the supernatural takes on your relationships; the people you care about and your real job all have ratings that decrease if not tended to... but that's time that could be spent on the hunt, or honing your skills, or in therapy. I'd love for HtV to steal that.<br /> <br /> The Vigil is not a path that normal people walk. Any sane individual tries to get as far away from the monsters as possible, not sprint towards them with a camcorder and a cheap handgun. You have a life that we assume you give a shit about, and hunting monsters is not reconcilable with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:19:10-08:00","id":794385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794354#post794354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that the upcoming edition of Delta Green stresses is the toll that hunting the supernatural takes on your relationships; the people you care about and your real job all have ratings that decrease if not tended to... but that's time that could be spent on the hunt, or honing your skills, or in therapy. I'd love for HtV to steal that.<br /> <br /> The Vigil is not a path that normal people walk. Any sane individual tries to get as far away from the monsters as possible, not sprint towards them with a camcorder and a cheap handgun. You have a life that we assume you give a shit about, and hunting monsters is not reconcilable with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why Hunters team up with like minded peers (their Cell). ...Which inevitably becomes their only real social group. It <i>becomes</i> their life.<br /> <br /> No wonder Cells trip so many &quot;they may be in a cult or fight club&quot; flags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T14:41:29-08:00","id":794395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794347#post794347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the movie Poltergeist, they realize something supernatural is happening in their home, things escalate, and in the end, they move and get rid of their tv, potentially living the rest of their lives, except for arguably some sequels, without involving the supernatural except perhaps tangentially. Fox Mulder, on the other hand, had an experience when he was a child and spent the rest of his life aggressively seeking the cause and other parallel issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which only seems to demonstrate my point. Poltergeist is one movie, with one story. The X-files was a long running TV show with 202 episodes, two movies, and an upcoming 6 part mini-series.<br /> <br /> Poltergeist isn't a long term game. It's a one-shot. The X-files is a long term game with dozens of individual stories between the massive myth-arc.<br /> <br /> If I'm going to be running a mortals game for ~50 sessions, I can't just do Poltergeist. Even if ghosts are the other supernatural antagonists in all 50 sessions, eventually the PCs are going to wise up to dealing with ghosts, and stop just doing what the family in Poltergeist did.<br /> <br /> This only furthers the idea that long running mortal games are inherently going to turn into Hunter games unless you keep the supernatural to an absolute minimum (and which point... why am I using the CofD?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters actively seek out the supernatural and put an end to its interference in things. Mortals try to live mortal lives, hunters don't. </div> </div> </div>What about the Union? Sure they seek out supernatural threats. But only local ones. Once they've clean up their neighborhoods of supernatural dangers, most turn towards local mortal dangers over going and looking for more supernaturals elsewhere. Trying to live their mortal lives is something most Union members consider important (it's explicitly part of their sell to get Tier 1 hunters to join up).<br /> <br /> You're trying to draw a bright line that doesn't really exist in the games as-is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can play long-term mortal games all you want, but if your characters are supernatural investigators, you would be better served by playing Hunter, that's what the game is for and there's more support for them within the system. </div> </div> </div>I don't see why there's an assumption that there's a universal optimal choice here. As has been noted, the core CofD book has more than enough support for running supernatural investigators that are equivalent to Tier 1 hunters. What does HtV currently offer? A few mechanical widgets that are very light on narrative impact. 1e Code simply isn't important (Mortal Remains explicitly says to just use Integrity). More options for WP expenditures, but a lot of them can be achieved through normal mortal Conditions, equipment, and Merits as well. Practical Beats/XP to get Tactics.<br /> <br /> In terms of actual support for supernatural investigations... that isn't much. WP goes a bit farther, and you get a limited ability to break the normal teamwork rules via Tactics.<br /> <br /> This is, again, why I went to the idea of having a Hunt Condition style idea. It's a way to separate what hunters do when they hunt from other beings. Just like the Sacred Hunt is a very different experience in play via its linked Conditions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:24:16-08:00","id":794418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794395#post794395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This only furthers the idea that long running mortal games are inherently going to turn into Hunter games unless you keep the supernatural to an absolute minimum (and which point... why am I using the CofD?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Games don't turn into other games unless you want them to. Like I said, you can run 'mortal' three sessions a week for ten years. But you would be better served to play hunter with them, because you are effectively playing hunter, providing you're running a steady game with the characters constantly hunting the supernatural. Mortal games are not forced to always interact with the supernatural, after all, and are capable of dealing with 'mundane' antagonists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about the Union? Sure they seek out supernatural threats. But only local ones. Once they've clean up their neighborhoods of supernatural dangers, most turn towards local mortal dangers over going and looking for more supernaturals elsewhere. Trying to live their mortal lives is something most Union members consider important (it's explicitly part of their sell to get Tier 1 hunters to join up).<br /> <br /> You're trying to draw a bright line that doesn't really exist in the games as-is. </div> </div> </div>If you'd please turn your Hunter core book to page 17, starting on line four. <br /> <br /> If you're in the Union, you're not just going out to kill a monster then never deal with it again like Tom Hanks in the Burbs, you're in the Union, you're actively part of an organization that hunts monsters. If you aren't going to be hunting monsters, mundane or magical, or assisting folks in doing so, then you wouldn't be in the Union, you'd just be a mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see why there's an assumption that there's a universal optimal choice here. As has been noted, the core CofD book has more than enough support for running supernatural investigators that are equivalent to Tier 1 hunters. What does HtV currently offer? A few mechanical widgets that are very light on narrative impact. 1e Code simply isn't important (Mortal Remains explicitly says to just use Integrity). More options for WP expenditures, but a lot of them can be achieved through normal mortal Conditions, equipment, and Merits as well. Practical Beats/XP to get Tactics.<br /> <br /> In terms of actual support for supernatural investigations... that isn't much. WP goes a bit farther, and you get a limited ability to break the normal teamwork rules via Tactics. </div> </div> </div>There's actually no support for supernatural organizations. Or any way to tell what the universal optimal choice is. Because second edition Hunter isn't available at all and there's not even a glimpse of what it's going to be about other than 'more slashers.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T15:41:38-08:00","id":794426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794304#post794304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that's a fairly weak response; mostly because it really doesn't seem to mesh with trying to run a long term mortals focused game. It's basically saying that all long term mortal games will turn into Tier 1 hunters, because after the nth time they've dealt with something supernatural and decided to stop being 100% reactive about the existence of more supernaturals out there, they're hunters. If you want to keep to a mortals game thematically... you have to make all the PCs stupid so they'll never start taking proactive steps to protect their normal life from the supernatural stuff they've encountered; lest they become a Tier 1 hunter for it.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons I thought of something like having something similar to the Sacred Hunt Conditions from Forsaken to give to hunters. Rather than some arbitrary line of reactive vs.proactive approach to the existence of the supernatural, hunters take dealing with the supernatural an extra step that's represented in how those Conditions are generated, and what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I can put it another way.<br /> <br /> One is a grimdark slice of life series, more problems than monsters, more strange places and times and items and wanderers than permanent residents twisting everything.<br /> The other is, at the minimum, a monster of the week series, possibly sequeing into grander monster conspiracies. Permanent residents definitely are twisting everything.<br /> <br /> One just wants to live with it, and deals with problems to return to normality. the other says &quot;Fuck normality&quot;, and deals with problems to resolve deeper issues.<br /> <br /> And I'm not positing my method is the answer for the entire game, but it works for my table. That said, look at the God-Machine Chronicle and how that fits my paradigm. I'm not drawing a line and saying &quot;this is the difference&quot;, but I am suggesting that the game is at least hinting that there's a difference of mentality between the two. There's room to disagree with me, of course-again, this is just my approach to the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T17:19:27-08:00","id":794484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794418#post794418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Games don't turn into other games unless you want them to....because you are effectively playing hunter...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but you're arguing contradictory things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortal games are not forced to always interact with the supernatural, after all, and are capable of dealing with 'mundane' antagonists. </div> </div> </div>So can Hunter... did you not consider this statement as the Union is also being discussed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you'd please turn your Hunter core book to page 17, starting on line four. </div> </div> </div>Which adds what to this? Yes, most of humanity chooses to ignore the supernatural for what it is. PCs, mortals or hunters, aren't most of humanity.<br /> <br /> Also, pleasure open a copy of the new CofD core book, and note the supernatural Merits, the ephemeral entities, and Horrors sections. Now consider the impact of having all of these in the core book on what mortal games are intended to interact with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're in the Union, you're not just going out to kill a monster then never deal with it again like Tom Hanks in the Burbs, you're in the Union, you're actively part of an organization that hunts monsters. If you aren't going to be hunting monsters, mundane or magical, or assisting folks in doing so, then you wouldn't be in the Union, you'd just be a mortal. </div> </div> </div>So... now we're shifting the goal posts? Or just getting highly circular that you're a hunter because you're in a hunter organization, and if you weren't doing things for the organization you'd get kicked out/retired and stop being a hunter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because second edition Hunter isn't available at all and there's not even a glimpse of what it's going to be about other than 'more slashers.' </div> </div> </div>This seems rather disingenuous. You're willing to making all sorts of definitive statements about what hunters are, but then retreat to, &quot;well 2e HtV isn't out yet.&quot; to dodge points on things that may or may not change in the new edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794426#post794426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm not positing my method is the answer for the entire game, but it works for my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, ultimately, unhelpful to me. And I'm going to assume to wyrdhamster as well.<br /> <br /> If I wanted advice for keeping them separate in my games... I'd ask for that. I'd rather discuss how the open-dev process can be used to examine the Tiers of HtV to see if there are ways to highlight the thematic differences more concretely so that a Tier 1 hunter group, and a main book mortal supernatural investigation group, feel different without ST/player enforcement of themes based on personal interpretations of how to segregate the two games.<br /> <br /> We have a lead dev. that has expressed interest in examining the role the Tiers play in this. How about we take it as a given that 1e HtV was not unquestionably successful in separating hunters from normal mortals interacting with the supernatural, and then look at what can be done beyond personal lines between them?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why this isn't getting across, but I'll be a bit direct on a few things:<br /> <br /> 1) <b>I want there to be a difference</b> between the mentality of the two character types.<br /> <br /> 2 I want the 2e book to use the chance of a new edition to actualize this mentality difference more concretely.<br /> <br /> 3) I do not want mortal supernatural investigators, and Tier 1 hunters, to blur in the books to the point where we need to fall back on STs to solve the difference in keeping them separate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T18:05:10-08:00","id":794511,"title":"","content":"The difference between the mentality of a Hunter and a mortal who wants to hunt/investigate monsters is essentially nothing, because it is that mentality that makes them a Hunter to begin with. Again, the only difference between a normal human and a Hunter is the decision to hunt. This isn't really anything special to be honest. It is no different than the decision to be a soldier, or the decision to be a doctor, or social worker. You've dedicated yourself to a certain profession for one reason or another, and you focus your life around that cause.<br /> <br /> Like I said in a previous post, the only things that set Tier 1 Hunters apart from normal people are the kind of skills, information, and equipment that their job forces them to acquire. But in the grand scope of things, it's not really that much different than any other profession. Doctors, artists, soldiers, etc. all have certain types of skills, information, and equipment they need to perform the job they've dedicated themselves to.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that when you're playing a Hunter, you're not the hero, you're not the chosen one, and you aren't any different than anyone else who has dedicated their lives to something. You're just a person doing what you feel you need to do. The only difference is that your chosen line of work is much more dangerous than most and almost always thankless with minimum rewards. It's a shitty job but someone has to do it.<br /> <br /> ...Or at least that's how I see it. Obviously you're looking for something different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T18:18:47-08:00","id":794517,"title":"","content":"I said you might as well be playing hunter if you choose to base your games around monster hunting. Mortal games are more open to other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794484#post794484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which adds what to this? Yes, most of humanity chooses to ignore the supernatural for what it is. PCs, mortals or hunters, aren't most of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It responds to your statement that my point that my 'line' isn't supported by the books. 'it's like a hangnail or a raw tooth: they can't leave it alone, picking at it no matter the pain.' P54, 'The Vigil is a choice: a very conscious, very obsessive, borderline insane choice to walk where angels fear to tread and, once upon the path, to remain there rather than run for the 'safety' of willful ignorance.' Basically wherever it explains what a hunter is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, pleasure open a copy of the new CofD core book, and note the supernatural Merits, the ephemeral entities, and Horrors sections. Now consider the impact of having all of these in the core book on what mortal games are intended to interact with. </div> </div> </div>It's more in how you interact with it. Supernatural merits don't make you a hunter, either do the existence of ephemeral entities or horrors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So... now we're shifting the goal posts? Or just getting highly circular that you're a hunter because you're in a hunter organization, and if you weren't doing things for the organization you'd get kicked out/retired and stop being a hunter? </div> </div> </div>There's no shifting of goalposts. I explained the difference between mortals and hunters to wyrdhamster. You claimed it was a weak response and suggested that all mortal games must become hunter games. But mortals can just bump into stuff. They can work for a shopkeeper whose menagerie of cursed relics was looted and wants them back. They can move out of their haunted house and into another haunted house. They can be sent on a mission to investigate ruins. They can try to reveal the organized crime-influenced corruption on the city council. They can have entire games about love triangles between mob bosses and serial killers. And they can hunt monsters. If you want to support those last characters, mechanically and in first edition, Hunter is a good way to do so, but you're under no obligation to use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're willing to making all sorts of definitive statements about what hunters are, but then retreat to, &quot;well 2e HtV isn't out yet.&quot; to dodge points on things that may or may not change in the new edition. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was making all sorts of definitive statements about what the difference between hunters and mortals are in first edition, like when I pointed at the first edition book where it says that they cannot let it go. Because that's an example of what the difference is between them. Mortal games can be played the same way as they can in first edition. You have your soap operas, your thrillers, mysteries, action, horror and even monster hunting. You decided to compare the Chronicles of Darkness book to Hunter's first edition, 'What does HtV currently offer?' And you've been told what it offers, but what second edition Hunter offers is entirely up in the air.<br /> <br /> As a side note, Tier 1 hunters are not any less part of the Vigil than those of the other tiers. They can't let it go either, they just aren't part of a larger organization that's focused on hunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T19:42:55-08:00","id":794562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794511#post794511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between the mentality of a Hunter and a mortal who wants to hunt/investigate monsters is essentially nothing, because it is that mentality that makes them a Hunter to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that can be held to be universally true. As nofather has been banging on about, hunters are suppposed to have a mental aspect that takes them beyond normal mortals that deal in the supernatural. You also have a few organizations (esp. in Tier 3) where there are background elements within the organization that add other mentality issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously you're looking for something different. </div> </div> </div>For the vast majority of what you said... not really?<br /> <br /> I'm looking for the uniquely dedicated/obsessive/etc. focus to dealing with the supernatural that is supposed to separate hunters from mortal supernatural investigators to be actualized between in HtV 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794517#post794517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said you might as well be playing hunter if you choose to base your games around monster hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is still arguing two exclusive positions. You're arguing that playing monster based mortal games is essentially the same as playing Tier 1 hunters, while you're also arguing that mortals and hunters have a fundamental difference in mentality. It can't be both. Either there's an inherent difference between normal mortal games that deal with a lot of supernatural threats and Hunter games based on that mentality, or there isn't actually a difference in mentality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It responds to your statement that my point that my 'line' isn't supported by the books. </div> </div> </div>It's missing the point then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You claimed it was a weak response and suggested that all mortal games must become hunter games. </div> </div> </div>No, I suggested your response (though not solely your response) forces a narrative that mortals in a supernatural heavy game must become a hunter game. You've yet to dissuade me from thinking this analysis is true. Even while citing how hunters aren't just mortals that combat the supernatural, you insist that mortals and Tier 1 hunters blur into each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You decided to compare the Chronicles of Darkness book to Hunter's first edition... </div> </div> </div>Including Mortal Remains...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you've been told what it offers,,, </div> </div> </div>Actually, I addressed it myself.<br /> <br /> Frankly you feel completely stuck on trying to &quot;correct&quot; something wrong on the Internet, that you've completely lost sight of what other people are saying, the coherence of your own statements, and what actually started all this. It is growing increasingly frustrating. I'd rather you take a breather and actually look at things with a bit a mental difference so we can discuss things, rather than circling back endlessly to you yelling about the differences between mortals and hunters as if it mattered to what wyrdhamster and I are actually concerned about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:00:50-08:00","id":794587,"title":"","content":"Asked to write, I want to point one thing in mortal games vs. Tier 1 <b>Hunter</b> here - <b>There should be some mechanical difference in Hunter 2ED, cause as it is, CoD corebook is more than enough to support &quot;hunters&quot; as it is - and this lead to Hunter's own Tier 1 fandom essentially do not need the 2ED Hunter corebook. </b>It is games problem, as main corebook is competing with the <b>Hunter</b> gameline on the same people to play with it. Or, in other words, <b>Hunter </b>2ED do not scream &quot;buy me&quot; for people interested in Tier 1 play if they have <b>CoD</b> corebook.<br /> <br /> This should be a goal of the Onyx Path to reach with new Hunter corebook - <b>to &quot;sell&quot; the Hunter game system as different thing and experience than main CoD mortal games. </b><br /> <br /> For now, it looks very weak. For sure we have only Risking Willpower unique mechanics in <b>Hunter</b>. Professions, Horror making, all the Ephemera Beings, supernatural Equipment, even rules for so fundamental <b>Hunter</b>-like scenes like Investigations and Chases or proto-Tactics ( as Plans in Building Equipement ) are in <b>CoD </b>corebook. As Tier 1 Hunter is all about &quot;we are all alone in this one&quot;, even setting groups are not needed to run it - from <b>Hunter</b> 1ED point of view. <b>That means that - as it is - Tier 1 Hunter is <i>not</i> needed in Hunter 2ED corebook, </b><br /> <br /> <b>But I want him to be</b> - I really want to make Tier 1 hunting a other activity than Monster of the Week mortal games.That rules support a larger differences. That characters <i>feel</i> different on first sight and I do not need to question &quot;is this mortal game or <b>Hunter</b> now?&quot;. <b>Surely there are things that distinguish Winchester brothers or Mulder and Scully from characters that choose to investigate monsters when they cross with them</b>. We just need to find those differences in to mechanics and we will have our answers how to make 2ED <b>Hunter</b> trully unique from <b>CoD</b> corebook.<br /> <br /> Mine propositions to add to Hunter template for Tier 1 ( and up ) games:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Code</b> - The base Integrity rules are a kind of problem for monster hunters. If every encounter with supernatural can diminish your Integrity, hunters would long ago ended all in mental asylums from confronting the Unknown. I see this in our <b><i>Mortal Remains</i> Hunter</b> game where after only 3 sessions two characters have lowered Integrity, only from encounter with supernatural. And this is where I think that Code can shine - hunters are not mortals, not in the psychological sense. They accept supernatural on the core level and decide to do something with it. Code mark that they are not &quot;normal&quot; now, and changing from Integrity to Code would mark transition in to proper hunter. It also nicely tie in with <i>Slasher Chronicle</i> angle, as more character is invested in to Code, the more closer they are in to Slasher territory of &quot;I must kill redheads&quot; kind a way. Slashers are creatures of habit and getting Code is first step to gaining those habits...<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Hunting Conditions</b> - I agree with <b>Heavy Arms</b> that something like werewolves Siskur-Dah Conditions would nicely tell apart mortals and hunters in their confrontation with monsters. Mortals are victim - victims that sometimes <i>want </i>to do something proactively - but they do not seek the monsters as hunters are. They do not <i>need</i> to fight the Darkness. Risking Willpower is steaming from the high the hunters are getting when confronting monsters. Why not dwell more in to it and say that can have some more mechanical effects when hunting? That, deep down, hunters <i>love</i> to hunt. That our Winchester brothers or Mulder and Scully <i>really</i> want to confront monsters and it get's them &quot;to the buttom of this&quot;. Mortal can all do this things if they need to - hunters should feel it is <i>good</i> for them. They should get a little high of adrenaline from confronting with Unknown. They <b><i>want</i></b> to hunt.<br /> <br /> I swear I had some third idea, but I cannot remember now...<br /> <br /> <b>So maybe you have other small points that different mortal investigators and proper hunters that could be made in to new mechanics for Tier 1 play?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-29-2015, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:29:17-08:00","id":794596,"title":"","content":"Gee, it's like I said my answer wasn't going to satisfy folks.<br /> <br /> We'll see what Monica has to say about it. For me, the blurring thing isn't a problem, but I can see how it is for other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:39:31-08:00","id":794601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794562#post794562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly you feel completely stuck on trying to &quot;correct&quot; something wrong on the Internet, that you've completely lost sight of what other people are saying, the coherence of your own statements, and what actually started all this. It is growing increasingly frustrating. I'd rather you take a breather and actually look at things with a bit a mental difference so we can discuss things, rather than circling back endlessly to you yelling about the differences between mortals and hunters as if it mattered to what wyrdhamster and I are actually concerned about.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to want an argument. Try someone else. The reason you might feel I'm 'stuck' on pointing out something is because that's all I was responding to in the first place. If you have a problem comprehending what I and others have said, it is made more clear by reading the Hunter book and the core World of Darkness books. A breather might be good for you as well, especially if you're getting so frustrated by arguing about my explanation to wyrdhamster.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T23:26:44-08:00","id":794641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794601#post794601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to want an argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I want people to actually engage with what other posters are saying in good faith. You aren't doing that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T01:51:26-08:00","id":794689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794562#post794562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that can be held to be universally true. As nofather has been banging on about, hunters are suppposed to have a mental aspect that takes them beyond normal mortals that deal in the supernatural. You also have a few organizations (esp. in Tier 3) where there are background elements within the organization that add other mentality issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the vast majority of what you said... not really?<br /> <br /> I'm looking for the uniquely dedicated/obsessive/etc. focus to dealing with the supernatural that is supposed to separate hunters from mortal supernatural investigators to be actualized between in HtV 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I don't really believe that to be unique. People can get intensely obsessive over pretty much anything, so being obsessive over this particular profession isn't really that special imo. Again, it's not really any different from the type of people who live and breathe a military lifestyle. Simply put, I don't really think that being mundanely obsessed with something (unless you want to argue it is some sort of inherently supernatural compulsion) justifies some sort of unique Condition or aspect, since this is really the kind of thing that anyone can have over anything. In fact, there's already an Obsession Condition made specifically for this kind of mentality. If you really want to represent some sort of overpowering dedication to a cause you could just use that, couldn't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T02:24:42-08:00","id":794703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794689#post794689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I don't really think that being mundanely obsessed with something (unless you want to argue it is some sort of inherently supernatural compulsion) justifies some sort of unique Condition or aspect, since this is really the kind of thing that anyone can have over anything. In fact, there's already an Obsession Condition made specifically for this kind of mentality. If you really want to represent some sort of overpowering dedication to a cause you could just use that, couldn't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2ED <b>Werewolf</b> you can also get Obsession Condition over your Prey, but we still get Siskur-Dah as pointing to the target and connected mechanics to it. Or in 2ED <b>Mage</b> you can easily have your Aspirations to work as Obsessions, not need second pool of those specially for this - but still some mechanical nuances to the game, to work better with it's themes.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter</b> should be about &quot;hunt&quot;, not just &quot;mortals in Chronicles of Darkness world&quot; - we, literally, has whole corebook about that in our PDF readers. ( Yes, it's called <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> corebook ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-29-2015, 05:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T02:34:57-08:00","id":794712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794689#post794689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I don't really think that being mundanely obsessed with something (unless you want to argue it is some sort of inherently supernatural compulsion) justifies some sort of unique Condition or aspect, since this is really the kind of thing that anyone can have over anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what's the point of having the HtV game line as a separate thing from blue book mortals? Why give it a full core book, special rules, and all that focus? Even if &quot;realistically&quot; there's nothing special about it, it is certainly special from a narrative perspective. You seem to be arguing for HtV 2e to really be CofD: Hunters as a supplement to the core book.<br /> <br /> If we accept the base premise (which is noted in the HtV 1e core book as cited previously by nofather) that being a hunter goes beyond the pale of normal people being obsessed with something, even if it isn't a supernatural compulsion, then that's what wyrmhamster and I are concerned about the game not presenting well holistically. If you reject that premise... you're kind of rejecting the premise of the game-line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you really want to represent some sort of overpowering dedication to a cause you could just use that, couldn't you? </div> </div> </div>Not for the specific design goals in question. The whole point is to show that hunters go above and beyond. Just hitting them all with ready access to the same normal Condition doesn't really accomplish that. It's also highly restrictive. One of the points of the comparison to the Siskur-Dah Condition is that how you get it matters to what it does. A Blood Talon's Sacred Hunt isn't the same as a Storm Lord's Sacred Hunt. If we kept to my spitball idea of having a specific set of hunt-starting Tactics, those Tactics would each generate different effects for hunters Keeping the Vigil (it would also, incidentally, help with cross-organization play depending on implementation*). A wider array of possible Conditions leads to a greater variety of play experiences, and more depth to individualizing an organization based on which hunt-starting Tactics it uses.<br /> <br /> * - This could be done &quot;exclusively&quot; where hunters need to have the same hunt-starting Tactic as the primary actor to benefit, which helps OOC pick organizations that have a certain amount of cross compatibility, or &quot;inclusively&quot; where any hunter involved in the opening can benefit, which gives greater cohesion to a more mixed organization PC group, and greater access to different Conditions to put up based on the nature of the enemy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T03:39:05-08:00","id":794737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to be arguing for HtV 2e to really be CofD: Hunters as a supplement to the core book. </div> </div> </div>For Tier 1 hunters it basically is already. The differentiation comes from the setting material not the ruleset, and Tier 1 is kinda the pre-setting stage where it's just your cell. The Hunter books give a pretty overwhelming focus on the compacts and conspiracies for a reason.<br /> <br /> I think the proposed rules are quite good and could be really interesting, but I don't see the need to insert new rules to justify Hunter being a seperate book line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T09:22:02-08:00","id":794891,"title":"","content":"Michael got to it before me, but yes, I do feel that Hunter is generally a blue book supplement for mortals who want to hunt monsters. They aren't a major template like the other lines, and unlike the major templates (and even a lot of minor templates) Hunter, at least Tier 1 Hunter, lacks anything to really separate them from normal mortals. Most of the things they get are things called out as being there to help give Hunter an extra boost to try to keep up with the things they hunt and usually brings attention to the fact that most of these things aren't really something that would logically be restricted to only Hunters. Even the narrative justification is fairly weak imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-29-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T12:36:49-08:00","id":795016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794737#post794737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The differentiation comes from the setting material not the ruleset, and Tier 1 is kinda the pre-setting stage where it's just your cell. The Hunter books give a pretty overwhelming focus on the compacts and conspiracies for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can see though, why some of us consider the differentiation only existing in setting material without mechanical support is a problem?<br /> <br /> And I don't think it does any good to down play the viability of Tier 1 play. Tier 1 play doesn't get a lot of focus because it's all about a single personalized organization, where Tier 2-3 play is about joining existing organizations. It takes more book space and focus to detail existing organizations to make them playable, than it takes to have a group that is an organization onto itself defined solely by the players. Starting at Tier 1 and moving to Tier 2 is clearly one thing you can do with the game, but just playing Tier 1 is supposed to be valid as well. It shouldn't be seen as just &quot;pre-setting.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the proposed rules are quite good and could be really interesting, but I don't see the need to insert new rules to justify Hunter being a seperate book line. </div> </div> </div>Then what does justify a new book line? Yes, rules alone do not (but as noted, we're talking about rules intended to support setting material that is already there without mechanical support). If HtV is supposed to be a separate book line.. it should have something that makes it worthy of this. Whatever that is, shouldn't it also have the rules to back it up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=794891#post794891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Michael got to it before me, but yes, I do feel that Hunter is generally a blue book supplement for mortals who want to hunt monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. But you can see that for those of us that don't want it to be that, because that's not how it is presented, it's a problem to treat it this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T14:46:51-08:00","id":795097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can see though, why some of us consider the differentiation only existing in setting material without mechanical support is a problem? </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand. The setting has lots of mechanical support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't think it does any good to down play the viability of Tier 1 play. Tier 1 play doesn't get a lot of focus because it's all about a single personalized organization, where Tier 2-3 play is about joining existing organizations. It takes more book space and focus to detail existing organizations to make them playable, than it takes to have a group that is an organization onto itself defined solely by the players. Starting at Tier 1 and moving to Tier 2 is clearly one thing you can do with the game, but just playing Tier 1 is supposed to be valid as well. It shouldn't be seen as just &quot;pre-setting.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean it in a viabilty sense. I meant it as you just laid it out there. There's just not that much for the writers to do. You lay out the core ideas of theme and mood, give a few extra rules and away you go. It's 'pre-setting' in the sense that Tier 1 hunters don't really seem to interact much with the hunter subculture; the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then what does justify a new book line? </div> </div> </div>Having enough material? The whim of the developer? What the intellectual property holder will put up with? The developers wanted to create a series of books that were very close to the core mortals game, but with a specialised focus and a heavily fleshed out setting. Calling it a line and giving it a cool name seems only sensible so people know what they're reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it should have something that makes it worthy of this. Whatever that is, shouldn't it also have the rules to back it up? </div> </div> </div>It should and it does. The rules just happen to largely be already available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T16:15:40-08:00","id":795158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795016#post795016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. But you can see that for those of us that don't want it to be that, because that's not how it is presented, it's a problem to treat it this way?</div> </div> </div> </div>A problem? No, but personally I'd like to see more of a justification for what puts them above blue book mortals other than some meta power boost and a 'but guys, they're really dedicated!'. I wouldn't mind Hunter specific material if it made sense why non-Hunters couldn't have access to it, but as the 1e Hunter core liked to point out so frequently about the 'unique' Hunter abilities, these are conceptually not things limited to just them. Yes, they happen to show up in their book, and yes, they happen to be designed for this gameline so give it a boost in effectiveness, but all of that is, again, fairly meta.<br /> <br /> Practical Experience is pretty much just extra experience given out just as a power boost for doing things that even mortal investigators do. Unless you want to argue that taking up the Vigil somehow magically enhances a characters ability to learn from the exact same type of things said character was doing as a blue book mortal before becoming a Hunter I'd just chalk this as a helpful boost based on an already abstract system. Risking Willpower is literally just performing some sort of desperate do-or-die maneuver, something pretty much anyone is able to do. Hell, the text all but says it's just a game balance thing. And Tactics? Do I even need to elaborate on Tactics? These are all things that anyone could theoretically learn, be they blue book mortals or even other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> All in all, even thematically, there's just not a big enough difference between Hunter and mortal for their to reasonably <i>be</i> a difference between Tier 1 and mortal investigators. So if anything, I would start there. I'd like to see a real difference added, something to actually make them more than their blue book counterparts. If they are to gain something that makes them inherently different than your normal everyday person, I'd love to see a real, unique, defining cause. Being obsessed and dedicated isn't enough in my mind, there are plenty of obsessed and dedicated people, but they (as far as I know at least), don't develop inherent advantages to set them apart from everyday people.<br /> <br /> And if it's not justified? Meh, I'll just shrug and wonder why whatever they it was added as a Hunter mechanic rather than just a base option for everybody, just like I did with professional training back in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T17:10:54-08:00","id":795205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795097#post795097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand. The setting has lots of mechanical support.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment, Tactics/PXP and Risking WP are the only two things that support Tier 1 hunters. I think I've spent a lot of time on why that's not sufficient. Is there something specific that was unclear in all that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's 'pre-setting' in the sense that Tier 1 hunters don't really seem to interact much with the hunter subculture; the setting. </div> </div> </div>But they <i>are</i> the hunter subculture. Tier rating doesn't change if you're part of the subculture or not, just the level of your organization. Cells are capable of - and noted as something that happens - interacting with each other, and with Compacts/Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It should and it does. The rules just happen to largely be already available. </div> </div> </div>I think it's pretty clear then that we disagree with &quot;it does.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795158#post795158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but personally I'd like to see more of a justification for what puts them above blue book mortals other than some meta power boost and a 'but guys, they're really dedicated!'. I wouldn't mind Hunter specific material if it made sense why non-Hunters couldn't have access to it, but as the 1e Hunter core liked to point out so frequently about the 'unique' Hunter abilities, these are conceptually not things limited to just them. Yes, they happen to show up in their book, and yes, they happen to be designed for this gameline so give it a boost in effectiveness, but all of that is, again, fairly meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind that. The problem is... what would it be? HtV fans aren't going to want it to move towards HtR and have an overtly supernatural source. The only real option that seems viable would be that some people are just &quot;special&quot; in the CofD, and respond to the supernatural lurking in the shadows as hunters leading to a mentality (and the rules behind it) that normal people just don't develop. Which is basically what things already are, but more explicit that hunters are some odd outlier group of humans that have something different in them. Which is still pretty meta.<br /> <br /> That said, how bad &quot;meta&quot; is, is highly subjective. I think most of the current HtV fanbase that values HtV as a full game line instead of a supplement to the blue books are far more comfortable with the meta-justifications that you are personally.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:10:32-08:00","id":795262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the moment, Tactics/PXP and Risking WP are the only two things that support Tier 1 hunters. I think I've spent a lot of time on why that's not sufficient. Is there something specific that was unclear in all that? </div> </div> </div>Ok. But the quote that you originally made in #68, I specifically ignored Tier 1 Hunters. That was my point. Hunter generally focuses on the Tier 2 &amp; 3 stuff.<br /> <br /> Ignoring the total miscommunication, I still don't know why you think it's insufficient. Your only argument seems to be one about differentiating the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:20:13-08:00","id":795272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795205#post795205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind that. The problem is... what would it be? HtV fans aren't going to want it to move towards HtR and have an overtly supernatural source. The only real option that seems viable would be that some people are just &quot;special&quot; in the CofD, and respond to the supernatural lurking in the shadows as hunters leading to a mentality (and the rules behind it) that normal people just don't develop. Which is basically what things already are, but more explicit that hunters are some odd outlier group of humans that have something different in them. Which is still pretty meta.<br /> <br /> That said, how bad &quot;meta&quot; is, is highly subjective. I think most of the current HtV fanbase that values HtV as a full game line instead of a supplement to the blue books are far more comfortable with the meta-justifications that you are personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the biggest issue I'm seeing with the entire thing. Hunters have <i>nothing</i> to distinguish them from blue book mortals, but that happens to be a big part of their charm. The fact that they aren't inherently supernatural of inhuman is a what makes them who they are, but it also makes it difficult to distinguish them from other mortals. I mean I guess you could go with the just saying that there are some people who are just mundanely special, but I don't really feel like anyone would be satisfied with that, myself included.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much this inability to legitimately make them special without making them so special that they lose what it is that makes them appealing that's led me to treating at them, at least low Tier members, as if they were just a natural extension of blue book mortals. Conceptually, Hunter for me is just a monster hunting supplement for blue book mortals on the same level as the psychics in Second Sight and the spoiled minor templates in the Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> As for the subjectivity of how meta something is, I fully understand that opinions will vary. The breaking point varies from person to person with each individual mechanic, and I don't mind some abstractions myself, like Practical Experience. But there's a point for me where you begin adding so much inherent junk to being a hunter that they're essentially supernatural themselves. I mean you can claim it's all &quot;mundane&quot;, but when it becomes crap that blue book mortals and other non-Hunters just can't attain it essentially starts to seem like magic, and again runs into the problem of going against what makes Hunter special. Or at least that's my opinion on it anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T19:22:28-08:00","id":795305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795262#post795262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. But the quote that you originally made in #68, I specifically ignored Tier 1 Hunters. That was my point. Hunter generally focuses on the Tier 2 &amp; 3 stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally this would have applied to Tier 2 as well. Tier 2 has gotten more as the game line progressed, though Mortal Remains has largely redone it as Status [Compact] is just the Hunter version of Mystery Cult Initiation, which loses it's punch as support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ignoring the total miscommunication, I still don't know why you think it's insufficient. Your only argument seems to be one about differentiating the game. </div> </div> </div>Losing the Code, and the expansion Endowments (unless you keep Endowments and the MCI style Status update, but I don't think that's how Mortal Remains wants it to work) in C&amp;C to Compacts are probably the two biggest issues at the moment in terms of 2e removing things that helped mechanically differentiate the games; esp. based on the mentality that is supposed to be the difference between them. I know other people feel that some other things (like Professional Training) should be included in that, but PT isn't really about being a hunter compared to the Code or Endowments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795272#post795272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty much this inability to legitimately make them special without making them so special that they lose what it is that makes them appealing that's led me to treating at them, at least low Tier members, as if they were just a natural extension of blue book mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm comfortable with the difficulty of a method of make them special that would appeal to most current HtV fans, being the same as a complete inability to make something legitimately special. I would personally be satisfied with the more as-is &quot;some are just mundanely special&quot; thing, because that's all I really need. The meta aspects don't bother me like you've expressed being bothered by them. That it wouldn't work for you doesn't mean it wouldn't be a legitimate solution; just not a practical solution if it would turn off too many people from the game (which seems like it will have to see what the Open Dev process dregs up as far as what a larger group or respondents than a few people on this thread say).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there's a point for me where you begin adding so much inherent junk to being a hunter that they're essentially supernatural themselves. I mean you can claim it's all &quot;mundane&quot;, but when it becomes crap that blue book mortals and other non-Hunters just can't attain it essentially starts to seem like magic, and again runs into the problem of going against what makes Hunter special. Or at least that's my opinion on it anyways. </div> </div> </div>I think it's a bit unfair to exclude a middle here. I mean, my suggestion (which obviously is an expression of what I'd like to see, and wyrmhamster seems pretty keen on), isn't really adding another widget to HtV. It's leveraging an already HtV exclusive system (Tactics) with a general 2e mechanic (Conditions), to help shape a different style/focus of game-play. So it seems a bit much to treat this as wanting all hunters to start to have multiple page Merit lists of borderline or outright supernatural bonuses ala the spoiled Hurt Locker minor templates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T19:30:35-08:00","id":795309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795305#post795305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit unfair to exclude a middle here. I mean, my suggestion (which obviously is an expression of what I'd like to see, and wyrmhamster seems pretty keen on), isn't really adding another widget to HtV. It's leveraging an already HtV exclusive system (Tactics) with a general 2e mechanic (Conditions), to help shape a different style/focus of game-play. So it seems a bit much to treat this as wanting all hunters to start to have multiple page Merit lists of borderline or outright supernatural bonuses ala the spoiled Hurt Locker minor templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with Tactics, is why should something as basic as that be a Hunter specific thing? This feels like one of those things, like with professional training, would benefit from being highly flexible and open to everyone. This is the kind of thing that is so widely applicable that it would fit in just as well with werewolves, mages, blue book mortals, and just about every organized group under the sun. This is partially what I'm talking about. Most Hunter stuff really doesn't feel like Hunter stuff. It is everybody stuff that just happens to have first shown up in a Hunter book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T19:52:47-08:00","id":795324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795305#post795305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a bit unfair to exclude a middle here. I mean, my suggestion (which obviously is an expression of what I'd like to see, and wyrmhamster seems pretty keen on), isn't really adding another widget to HtV. It's leveraging an already HtV exclusive system (Tactics) with a general 2e mechanic (Conditions), to help shape a different style/focus of game-play. So it seems a bit much to treat this as wanting all hunters to start to have multiple page Merit lists of borderline or outright supernatural bonuses ala the spoiled Hurt Locker minor templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters, in reality, <i>are</i> Lesser Template ( with Conspiracy guys being Minor ). They are on the same footing like spoiled today The Plain - mostly it's &quot;special techniques&quot;, maybe element or two supernatural. And this is <i>totally</i> okay - they still are human and &quot;mortal&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just think that mechanics should be putted more emphasis that Vigil is not &quot;we are mortals and shoot to monsters&quot; and that being hunter <b>is</b> kinda special state, where you are partially free from the Quiescence/Lunacy/etc. New version of Code should take care of this - other way we risk of truly unstable hunters all the time from confrontation with Unknown. Also, nicely could it be made as first step in to Slashdom...<br /> <br /> I would leave Practical EXP and Tactics all along - I just pointing they are kinda &quot;special special&quot;. Tactics your cell need to learn &quot;hard way&quot;, and need to practice them - so they natural stuff of &quot;late Tier 1, beginning Tier 2 &amp; 3&quot; gameplay. There is problem for starting and continuing of Tier 1 play here, as I see in our own Tier 1 Hunter chronicle. But I found solution! Making &quot;Plans&quot; as Building Equipment ( ones again, from <b>CoD</b> corebook ) - they sound as &quot;not tested Tactics&quot; and should be totally used as this - I plan to talk over with our Hunter ST on next session about Plans. Your cell want to set fire nicely some vampire, but never used this particular Tactic? Let them made &quot;Plan&quot; on this, and use this bonus on first try. Later just let them practice it in downtime and buy Tactics.<br /> <br /> I would also add Conditions to mark that &quot;hunt&quot; is a <b><i>life</i></b> for the hunters. Many posters say that difference between normal mortals and hunters is in narrative - well, Conditions are mechanics for putting narratives pieces in them, so let's use them as such. Mark that our hunters <i><b>are</b></i> special compered to mortal investigators by drive, experience and a bit screw on Integrity. And give us some nice chained Condition there, that will outline much more the hunt itself, compared to mortal investigators &quot;take shotguns and point in to heads&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795309#post795309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Tactics, is why should something as basic as that be a Hunter specific thing? This feels like one of those things, like with professional training, would benefit from being highly flexible and open to everyone. This is the kind of thing that is so widely applicable that it would fit in just as well with werewolves, mages, blue book mortals, and just about every organized group under the sun. This is partially what I'm talking about. Most Hunter stuff really doesn't feel like Hunter stuff. It is everybody stuff that just happens to have first shown up in a Hunter book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or because hunters are only one that have free XP to buy it, as they do not have other things to buy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-30-2015, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T21:13:29-08:00","id":795368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795309#post795309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Tactics, is why should something as basic as that be a Hunter specific thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... I get it. You're not happy with the whole, &quot;anything that is Hunter specific, and isn't an Endowment, isn't accessible to blue book mortals.&quot; state of things.<br /> <br /> You're not really helping move the conversation anywhere by moving from saying that at least some level of Hunter specific mechanics is OK, to assailing the ones that already exist.<br /> <br /> It's also kind of silly to say you're OK with PXP... but then question one of the main uses of PXP.<br /> <br /> And Tactics aren't exactly &quot;basic.&quot; They're an advanced application of the basic rules (essentially combining the normal teamwork rules which don't allow secondary actors to use different dice-pools from the primary actor like Tactics do, with what is now formally part of the crafting system in the new CofD core).<br /> <br /> And while Tactics are specific to Hunter, there are other ways to access similar things. Everyone can by Merits like Small Unit Tactics, and Formation Tactics (though needs 2e redo). Swarm Tactics has a very odd prerequisite of Carthian Status 1 to use it, but that makes even less sense that HtV Tactics being Hunter specific. Building Plan equipment is something open to everyone as well. Werewolves have their own tactics rules that emphasize the pack, and it's supernatural nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T22:46:29-08:00","id":795407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795368#post795368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok... I get it. You're not happy with the whole, &quot;anything that is Hunter specific, and isn't an Endowment, isn't accessible to blue book mortals.&quot; state of things.<br /> <br /> You're not really helping move the conversation anywhere by moving from saying that at least some level of Hunter specific mechanics is OK, to assailing the ones that already exist.<br /> <br /> It's also kind of silly to say you're OK with PXP... but then question one of the main uses of PXP.<br /> <br /> And Tactics aren't exactly &quot;basic.&quot; They're an advanced application of the basic rules (essentially combining the normal teamwork rules which don't allow secondary actors to use different dice-pools from the primary actor like Tactics do, with what is now formally part of the crafting system in the new CofD core).<br /> <br /> And while Tactics are specific to Hunter, there are other ways to access similar things. Everyone can by Merits like Small Unit Tactics, and Formation Tactics (though needs 2e redo). Swarm Tactics has a very odd prerequisite of Carthian Status 1 to use it, but that makes even less sense that HtV Tactics being Hunter specific. Building Plan equipment is something open to everyone as well. Werewolves have their own tactics rules that emphasize the pack, and it's supernatural nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonono, see, the only thing I have a problem with is Hunter specific things that don't make sense <i>being</i> Hunter specific. I bring it up again because it's a perfect example, but Professional Training, it didn't make sense being a Hunter thing in 1e. I'm so glad they fixed it for 2e, because there was literally no reason for other people not to have such a thing. Tactics sits in a similar place, where it is Hunter specific but doesn't really make sense being Hunter specific. Now I can imagine <i>certain</i> Hunter specific Tactics based around the things they do, but the base mechanic itself being restricted is completely nonsensical to me.<br /> <br /> And I wouldn't be 'assailing' the current Hunter specific mechanics if they made sense being Hunter specific. Yes, I'm ok with restricted content, but only <i>if those restrictions make sense</i>. A lot of the current Hunter mainstays simply don't. And since you mentioned it, I'm totally fine with the various Endowments, Benedictions, and other specific content in the book. Those make sense, there is a <i>reason</i> why Average Joe Mortal can't access or doesn't readily know how to use those.<br /> <br /> I'm ok with PXP because XP is such a heavily abstracted concept in the game world that that slight modification to it doesn't really change the nature between what Hunters are or establish weird artificial limits as to what everyday people are and are not capable of.<br /> <br /> Tactics are <i>pretty</i> basic, relatively speaking. You learn them and design them like any other sort of real life training. The military, the police, hell, even sports teams design, learn, or practice these sorts of things everyday. Yes, it's a more detailed execution of a previously simplified system, but so was the social maneuvering system, and like the social maneuvering system, what it covers is a fairly basic concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T03:21:51-08:00","id":796713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=795407#post795407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonono, see, the only thing I have a problem with is Hunter specific things that don't make sense <i>being</i> Hunter specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you're not actually leaving room for anything besides Endowments in the group of things that you consider making sense as being Hunter specific.<br /> <br /> You've stated that WP risking doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> You've stated Tactics doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> You've said that PXP makes sense... but without risking WP or Tactics, it's really only useful for buying Skills and Merits, but generates at an extremely slow pace (esp. if WP risking and Tactics were universalized and stop generating PXP). With the Mortal Remains update, banking enough to get the PXP for a new Tactic could be pretty easily accomplished in one or two fairly intense scenes. But divided equally towards normal trait improvement wouldn't even generate enough for 1 XP's worth of purchases for five PCs. If PXP is only useful for buying Skills and Merits... it's basically one more XP every 1-3 sessions if divided equally among five players.<br /> <br /> The Code, as it stands, is Integrity but killing monsters don't count as a breaking point (which probably doesn't even need to be said given we're dealing with hunters anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I bring it up again because it's a perfect example, but Professional Training, it didn't make sense being a Hunter thing in 1e. </div> </div> </div>I'm curious why you're assuming it was ever intended to be a &quot;Hunter thing&quot; back in 1e. 1e had lots of Merits that were introduced in various books that (1) didn't actually list prerequisites that would deny them to things outside the books purview, (2) made sense to allow for other things, and (3) plenty of developers and authors at the time were pretty clear they weren't meant to be exclusive, but they just hadn't thought of them until that point.<br /> <br /> I'd wager you're conflating the Professions section with the Merit itself. The Merit never specifies that it is Hunter exclusive, or that it is necessary to have professions. The Professions section is Hunter specific. Hunter puts lots of stress on professions because it matters a lot more to Hunter than most of the other game lines, though the level of detail it put on it was fairly wasteful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I'm ok with restricted content, but only <i>if those restrictions make sense</i>. </div> </div> </div>But your essentially insisting that they have to make sense based on a subjective assessment of &quot;realism&quot; in terms of whether or not anyone could theoretically achieve the same effect (and generally ignoring with Tactics that Tactics really don't let you do things other people can't do, just do them more easily). Genre, narrative, and similar conventions don't count... unless it's something super abstract to another subjective point of &quot;it not mattering any more.&quot; It's basically a position that means you can always say, &quot;Whatever my personal preference is? That's clearly the best choice.&quot; It either has to make sense to you, or be abstract enough to you that it doesn't matter if it makes sense or not. I could sit here and bang out a 10 page essay that marvelously argues for Tactics being abstract enough they don't, &quot;change the nature of what hunters are, or establish weird artificial limits as to what everyday people are and are not capable of,&quot; but you can just dismiss it all as not making enough sense on the realism angle.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, at this point, what are you trying to say/prove/whatever?<br /> <br /> We don't agree on what would be good for HtV to make it the game we'd each like. You're not selling me on your position (you're not trying, which is cool), but all you seem to be doing is restating your position ad nauseum. To what end?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-30-2015, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:01:38-08:00","id":796874,"title":"","content":"How long does this arbitrary semantic debate need to continue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:14:04-08:00","id":796882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=796874#post796874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does this arbitrary semantic debate need to continue?</div> </div> </div> </div>this is the internet. Making arbitrary semantic debates is its all shtick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:28:20-08:00","id":796889,"title":"","content":"And meta-snark totally improves things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T10:42:07-08:00","id":796897,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Thousands of 4channers can't be wro-nope, sorry, can't say it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T11:41:48-08:00","id":796926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/786793-light-your-candle?p=796713#post796713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you're not actually leaving room for anything besides Endowments in the group of things that you consider making sense as being Hunter specific.<br /> <br /> You've stated that WP risking doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> You've stated Tactics doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> You've said that PXP makes sense... but without risking WP or Tactics, it's really only useful for buying Skills and Merits, but generates at an extremely slow pace (esp. if WP risking and Tactics were universalized and stop generating PXP). With the Mortal Remains update, banking enough to get the PXP for a new Tactic could be pretty easily accomplished in one or two fairly intense scenes. But divided equally towards normal trait improvement wouldn't even generate enough for 1 XP's worth of purchases for five PCs. If PXP is only useful for buying Skills and Merits... it's basically one more XP every 1-3 sessions if divided equally among five players.<br /> <br /> The Code, as it stands, is Integrity but killing monsters don't count as a breaking point (which probably doesn't even need to be said given we're dealing with hunters anyway).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm curious why you're assuming it was ever intended to be a &quot;Hunter thing&quot; back in 1e. 1e had lots of Merits that were introduced in various books that (1) didn't actually list prerequisites that would deny them to things outside the books purview, (2) made sense to allow for other things, and (3) plenty of developers and authors at the time were pretty clear they weren't meant to be exclusive, but they just hadn't thought of them until that point.<br /> <br /> I'd wager you're conflating the Professions section with the Merit itself. The Merit never specifies that it is Hunter exclusive, or that it is necessary to have professions. The Professions section is Hunter specific. Hunter puts lots of stress on professions because it matters a lot more to Hunter than most of the other game lines, though the level of detail it put on it was fairly wasteful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But your essentially insisting that they have to make sense based on a subjective assessment of &quot;realism&quot; in terms of whether or not anyone could theoretically achieve the same effect (and generally ignoring with Tactics that Tactics really don't let you do things other people can't do, just do them more easily). Genre, narrative, and similar conventions don't count... unless it's something super abstract to another subjective point of &quot;it not mattering any more.&quot; It's basically a position that means you can always say, &quot;Whatever my personal preference is? That's clearly the best choice.&quot; It either has to make sense to you, or be abstract enough to you that it doesn't matter if it makes sense or not. I could sit here and bang out a 10 page essay that marvelously argues for Tactics being abstract enough they don't, &quot;change the nature of what hunters are, or establish weird artificial limits as to what everyday people are and are not capable of,&quot; but you can just dismiss it all as not making enough sense on the realism angle.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, at this point, what are you trying to say/prove/whatever?<br /> <br /> We don't agree on what would be good for HtV to make it the game we'd each like. You're not selling me on your position (you're not trying, which is cool), but all you seem to be doing is restating your position ad nauseum. To what end?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that the themes of Hunter don't leave much room. The game thematically wants to be about people with nothing substantially distinguishing themselves from normal people, yet asks for mechanics to show that they aren't like normal people. Do you see the problem there? It's a game about skilled normal people asking for mechanics to clearly show that they are not just skilled normal people. And not only that, but it tries to do so by introducing Hunter specific mechanics that the line itself acknowledges doesn't really make sense being Hunter specific due to how basic they are.<br /> <br /> Simply put, it feels like the line needs to decide whether Hunters are normal albeit highly skilled people, or if they possess some sort of beyond human attribute that lets them do things that highly skilled non-Hunters are incapable of replicating. It needs to specify what that attribute is and make mechanics thematically centered around it. And if they choose to not have anything really separating Hunters and highly skilled, high dedicated non-Hunters, there is little reason to have anything that is inherently restricted to Hunters. For example, even if they introduce it in a Hunter book, Tactics should be a general modification to the base system in the same manner as social maneuvering with most of the example Tactics being tailored to Hunters. <br /> <br /> As for why I thought Professional Training was a Hunter thing, it was due to not having read the exact text in a long time and the text on pg. 75 saying these professions were specifically for Hunter characters, with their only real mechanics being from the merit. And of course this is all opinion, but that's what this is all about, We've all been discussing our opinions on how we think things should be. I'm just stating my opinion, which seems to disagree with yours. You reply to my opinion with your argument and I counter with the reason my opinion is as such. So as for my goals? I don't have any! I came to state my opinion on the subject and happened to end up in a discussion concerning them. I've no intention of seriously trying to change your mind on the subject because you seem to be pretty set in your opinions and I don't quite care enough to try to convince you. I'm just enjoying the conversation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}